The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
wq = kzalloc(sizeof(*wq) + tbl_size, GFP_KERNEL);
if (!wq->unbound_attrs)
    goto err_free_wq;
```
Reason:
The bug occurs because when `alloc_workqueue` fails to allocate `unbound_attrs`, it jumps to the `err_free_wq` label without properly unregistering and freeing the lock dependency keys associated with the workqueue. This results in a use-after-free condition when the workqueue structure is accessed after it has been freed.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
wq_unregister_lockdep(wq);
wq_free_lockdep(wq);
```
Reason:
These statements ensure that the lock dependency keys associated with the workqueue are properly unregistered and freed before the workqueue structure itself is freed. This prevents the use-after-free condition by ensuring that all resources are cleaned up correctly when an error occurs during the allocation process.

